-- title:
--   Level Nrp unit-root refinement package at p
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $\mathcal O$ is a discrete valuation ring which is a domain of characteristic $0$, adically complete for its maximal ideal and with finite residue field $k=\mathrm{ResidueField}\,\mathcal O$; $p$ is a prime with $p\neq 2$ and $p\in\mathfrak m_{\mathcal O}$ (hypotheses `hp2`, `hp𝒪`).
--
--   *Residual representation.* $\bar\rho$ is a [`ResidualGaloisRep`](def/GaloisRep_Residual.html#L22) over $k$: a $k$-vector space $V$ of dimension $2$ together with a monoid homomorphism $\bar\rho.\rho$ from $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)=(\overline{\mathbb Q}\simeq_{\mathbb Q}\overline{\mathbb Q})$ to $\mathrm{End}_k V$ which is trivial on the automorphisms fixing some finite extension of $\mathbb Q$ inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}$. It is assumed absolutely irreducible (`habs`: the base change of $\bar\rho$ to $\overline k$ has no invariant submodule other than $\bot$ and $\top$) and ordinary at $p$ (`hord`): for every valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $p$ a non-unit in $P$ there is a $k$-line $L\subseteq V$, spanned by a member of a basis, stable under the decomposition subgroup of $P$, with $\bar\rho(\sigma)v-v\in L$ for all $v\in V$ and all $\sigma$ in the inertia subgroup of $P$.
--
--   *Level and ramification data.* $S$ is a finite set of primes (`hS`) containing $p$ (`hpS`); $N$ is a non-zero natural number, with $N p$ also non-zero, prime to $p$ (`hpN`), all of whose prime divisors lie in $S$ (`hNS`). $S_{\min}\subseteq S$ contains $p$ (`hpSmin`, `hSmin`) and, for primes $q\neq p$, $q\in S_{\min}$ holds exactly when $\bar\rho$ is ramified at $q$, i.e. when some $\sigma$ in some inertia group at $q$ acts non-trivially (`hmin`). Further: every $q\in S_{\min}$ with $q\neq p$ divides $N$ (`hNmin`); a prime $q\neq p$ dividing $N$ and not in $S_{\min}$ satisfies $q^2\mid N$ (`hNunr`); no prime $q\neq p$ has $q^3\mid N$ (`hN3`); and for $q\in S_{\min}$, $q\neq p$, the representation is unipotent on inertia at $q$, meaning that the characteristic polynomial of $\bar\rho(\sigma)$ is $(X-1)^2$ for every $\sigma$ in an inertia group at $q$ (`htame`).
--
--   *Auxiliary prime.* $r$ is a prime with $r\geq 5$, $r\notin S$, $r\nmid Np$ and $p\nmid r-1$ (`hr`, `hr5`, `hrS`, `hrN`, `hr1`), satisfying the no-level-raising condition `hrρ`: for every valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lying over $r$ and every $\sigma$ which is a Frobenius at $r$ for $P$ (i.e. lies in the decomposition group and acts on the residue field of $P$ by $x\mapsto x^{r}$), $(\operatorname{tr}\bar\rho(\sigma))^2\neq (r+1)^2$ in $k$.
--
--   *Eigensystems and $\mathcal O$-points.* Weight-two cusp forms of level $Np$ and of level $N$ are assumed to have an integral structure, i.e. the $\mathbb C$-span of the $\mathbb Z$-lattice of forms with integral $q$-expansion coefficients is everything. Ring homomorphisms $\theta_1\colon \mathbb T^{S}(Np)\to k$ and $\theta_0\colon\mathbb T^{S}(N)\to k$ are given on the Hecke algebras [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra (N*p) 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) and [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) (the $\mathbb Z$-subalgebras of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb C}$ of weight-two cusp forms on $\Gamma_0$ generated by the $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell$ outside $S$ not dividing the level and the $U_q$ for primes $q$ outside $S$ dividing the level), subject to `hθ₁` and `hθ₀`: for every prime $\ell$ outside $S$ not dividing the respective level, and every Frobenius $\sigma$ at $\ell$ attached to a valuation subring over $\ell$, the characteristic polynomial of $\bar\rho(\sigma)$ equals $X^2-\theta_i(T_\ell)X+\ell$. Moreover $\pi_{T_0}$ and $\pi_{T_1}$ are $\mathcal O$-algebra homomorphisms to $\mathcal O$ from [`CuspForm.heckeLocal N S 𝒪 θ₀`](def/CuspForm_HeckeLocal.html#L131) and [`CuspForm.heckeLocal (N*p) S 𝒪 θ₁`](def/CuspForm_HeckeLocal.html#L131) (the localisations of the $\mathcal O$-Hecke algebras at the primes cut out by $\theta_0$, $\theta_1$), agreeing on the images of the $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell\notin S$ with $\ell\nmid Np$ (`hπ`).
--
--   *The group $H_0$.* $H_0\leq (\mathbb Z/Nr)^\times$ is, by `hH₀`, exactly the kernel of reduction to $(\mathbb Z/r)^\times$, and $Nr\neq 0$.
--
--   *The level-$Nr$ corner datum.* $\mathbb T_0$ is a commutative ring and $\mathcal O$-algebra acting on $H^1(Nr,H_0;\mathcal O)$, the group of additive maps from the multiplicative group $\Gamma_{H_0}(Nr)\subseteq \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z)$ (written additively) to $\mathcal O$, compatibly with the $\mathcal O$-action. $S_0$ is an `IdempotentSplitting` of $\mathbb T_0$: a finite family of complete orthogonal idempotents $e_i$ together with maximal ideals $\mathfrak m_i$ exhausting all maximal ideals, with $e_i\in\mathfrak m_j$ if and only if $i\neq j$; $i_0$ is one of its indices, and $e_0$ is an $\mathcal O$-algebra isomorphism from the corner ring $S_0.\mathrm{CornerRing}\,i_0$ onto [`CuspForm.heckeLocal N S 𝒪 θ₀`](def/CuspForm_HeckeLocal.html#L131). The corner submodule $e_{i_0}\cdot H^1(Nr,H_0;\mathcal O)$ is assumed finite and free over $\mathcal O$. An element $t_p$ of the corner ring is given, and the remaining hypotheses on this datum are: `hT₀`, that for every prime $\ell$ with $\ell\nmid N$, $\ell\notin S$, $\ell\nmid Nr$ the element $e_0^{-1}(\pi(T_\ell))$ acts on the corner submodule as the operator `heckeT (N*r) H₀ ℓ 𝒪`; `htp`, that $t_p$ is a unit and acts on the corner submodule both as `heckeT (N*r) H₀ p 𝒪` and as `heckeTlower (N*r) H₀ p 𝒪`; `hocc₀`, that the submodule of the corner submodule annihilated by the kernel ideal of $\pi_{T_0}\circ e_0$ is non-zero; `hrk₀`, that the $\mathcal O$-rank of the corner submodule is the product of the $\mathcal O$-rank of that annihilated submodule with the $\mathcal O$-rank of the corner ring; `hgen`, that every element of $\mathbb T_0$ acts on $H^1(Nr,H_0;\mathcal O)$ through an element of the $\mathcal O$-subalgebra generated by the operator family [`CohCarrier.opFamily (N*r) H₀ S 𝒪`](def/CohCarrier_Inst.html#L91) indexed by [`CohCarrier.Gen (N*r) S`](def/CohCarrier_Inst.html#L13) (generators $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell\notin S$ not dividing $Nr$, $U_q$ for primes $q\mid Nr$, and diamonds $\langle d\rangle$); a lift $t^{\mathrm{full}}$ of that family to $\mathbb T_0$ and residual scalars $c^{\mathrm{full}}$ in $\mathcal O$ with, for all admissible generators $g$ — those for which the side condition holds, namely $q\mid N$ for a generator $U_q$ and no condition for $T_\ell$ and the diamonds — the action of $t^{\mathrm{full}}(g)$ on $H^1$ being that of `opFamily` at $g$ (`htfull`) and $t^{\mathrm{full}}(g)-c^{\mathrm{full}}(g)\in S_0.\mathfrak m\,i_0$ (`hcfull`); the co-fullness hypothesis `hcofull`, that a class $v$ lies in the corner submodule as soon as for each admissible $g$ and each $k$ some power $(t^{\mathrm{full}}(g)-c^{\mathrm{full}}(g))^n$ carries $v$ into $\mathfrak m_{\mathcal O}^k\cdot H^1(Nr,H_0;\mathcal O)$; `hcSigma`, that $c^{\mathrm{full}}(U_q)\in\mathfrak m_{\mathcal O}$ for every prime $q\mid Nr$ with $q\mid N$, $q\neq p$ and $q^2\mid N$; `hfaith₀`, that the corner ring acts faithfully on the corner submodule; and `hdia`, that `diamondRaw (N*r) H₀ 𝒪 σ` fixes every element of the corner submodule, for every $\sigma\in\Gamma_0(Nr)$.
--
--   *Unit root.* Finally $\alpha$ is an element of $S_0.\mathrm{CornerRing}\,i_0$ which (`hαt`) is a unit, satisfies $\alpha^2-t_p\alpha+p=0$, and has $\alpha-t_p$ in the ideal generated by the image of $\mathfrak m_{\mathcal O}$.
--
--   Under these assumptions, $Nrp\neq 0$ and there exist: a subgroup $H\leq(\mathbb Z/Nrp)^\times$ equal to the preimage of $H_0$ under reduction $(\mathbb Z/Nrp)^\times\to(\mathbb Z/Nr)^\times$; commutative rings $\mathbb T_a$, $\mathbb T_1$, each an $\mathcal O$-algebra, module-finite over $\mathcal O$, and each acting on $H^1(Nrp,H;\mathcal O)$ compatibly with $\mathcal O$; an $\mathcal O$-algebra homomorphism $\iota\colon\mathbb T_a\to\mathbb T_1$ with $\iota(t)\cdot v=t\cdot v$ for all $t$ and all $v\in H^1(Nrp,H;\mathcal O)$; an element $U\in\mathbb T_1$ acting as `heckeT (N*r*p) H p 𝒪`, such that the $\mathcal O$-subalgebra generated by the image of $\iota$ together with $U$ is all of $\mathbb T_1$; idempotent splittings $S_a$ of $\mathbb T_a$ with an index $i_a$ and $S_1$ of $\mathbb T_1$ with an index $i_1$; an $\mathcal O$-algebra isomorphism $e_1\colon S_1.\mathrm{CornerRing}\,i_1\xrightarrow{\ \sim\ }$ [`CuspForm.heckeLocal (N*p) S 𝒪 θ₁`](def/CuspForm_HeckeLocal.html#L131); both corner submodules $e_{i_a}\cdot H^1(Nrp,H;\mathcal O)$ and $e_{i_1}\cdot H^1(Nrp,H;\mathcal O)$ finite and free over $\mathcal O$; a witness $h_{1a}$ for `LevelLE (N*r*p) (N*r*p) ⊤ H 1` (namely $Nrp\mid Nrp$, $1\mid 1$, and $H$ maps into $\top$ under the identity reduction); and maps $t_A$ from [`CohCarrier.Gen (N*r) S`](def/CohCarrier_Inst.html#L13) to $\mathbb T_a$ and $d_A$ from $(\mathbb Z/Nrp)^\times$ to $\mathbb T_a$, for which all of the following hold.
--
--   First, for every generator $g$ satisfying the side condition (unrestricted for the $T_\ell$, the requirement $q\mid N$ for $U_q$, and never satisfied for a diamond), $t_A(g)$ acts on $H^1(Nrp,H;\mathcal O)$ as `heckeT (N*r*p) H ℓ 𝒪` when $g=T_\ell$, as `heckeT (N*r*p) H q 𝒪` when $g=U_q$, and as the identity in the diamond case. Second, for those same $g$, $t_A(g)-c^{\mathrm{full}}(g)\in S_a.\mathfrak m\,i_a$. Third, $d_A(d)$ acts as `diamondL (N*r*p) H 𝒪 d` for every $d\in(\mathbb Z/Nrp)^\times$. Fourth, $d_A(d)-1\in S_a.\mathfrak m\,i_a$ for every such $d$. Fifth, the $\mathcal O$-subalgebra of $\mathbb T_a$ generated by the values of $t_A$ on the admissible generators together with the whole image of $d_A$ is all of $\mathbb T_a$.
--
--   Sixth, every element of the corner submodule of $S_a.e\,i_a$ lies in the image, under the degeneracy map `iDegL (N*r*p) (N*r*p) ⊤ H 1 𝒪 𝒪 h₁ₐ`, of the submodule of parabolic homomorphisms on $\Gamma_{\top}(Nrp)$, i.e. of those $\mathcal O$-valued homomorphisms vanishing on every element whose trace squared equals $4$.
--
--   Seventh, the contraction of $S_1.\mathfrak m\,i_1$ along $\iota$ is $S_a.\mathfrak m\,i_a$, and $U\notin S_1.\mathfrak m\,i_1$. Eighth, for every $a\in\mathcal O$, if $\alpha-a$ lies in the maximal ideal of $S_0.\mathrm{CornerRing}\,i_0$ then $U-a\in S_1.\mathfrak m\,i_1$. Ninth, the corner submodule of $S_1.e\,i_1$ is contained in that of $S_a.e\,i_a$.
--
--   Tenth, there is a surjective $\mathcal O$-algebra homomorphism $\varphi\colon S_a.\mathrm{CornerRing}\,i_a\to S_1.\mathrm{CornerRing}\,i_1$ compatible with the two actions, in the sense that whenever $x$ in the corner submodule of $S_a.e\,i_a$ and $x_1$ in that of $S_1.e\,i_1$ have the same underlying class in $H^1(Nrp,H;\mathcal O)$, the classes of $t\cdot x$ and $\varphi(t)\cdot x_1$ coincide for every $t$; and such that for every prime $\ell$ with $\ell\nmid Np$, $\ell\notin S$, $\ell\nmid Nrp$, the element $e_1^{-1}(\pi(T_\ell))$ acts on the corner submodule of $S_1.e\,i_1$ as `heckeT (N*r*p) H ℓ 𝒪`.
--
--   Eleventh, $S_1.\mathrm{CornerRing}\,i_1$ acts faithfully on its corner submodule. Twelfth, the submodule of that corner submodule annihilated by the kernel ideal of $\pi_{T_1}\circ e_1$ is non-zero. Thirteenth, the $\mathcal O$-rank of the corner submodule of $S_1.e\,i_1$ equals the product of the $\mathcal O$-rank of that annihilated submodule with the $\mathcal O$-rank of $S_1.\mathrm{CornerRing}\,i_1$. Fourteenth, the submodule $\ker(\pi_{T_1}\circ e_1)\cdot(\text{corner submodule})$ is saturated: for $a\in\mathcal O$ non-zero and $m'$ in the corner submodule, $a\cdot m'$ belonging to it forces $m'$ to belong to it.
--
--   This is the level-$Nrp$ half of the Hecke-side rung at $p$ in the ordinary modularity-lifting argument: it transports a given local cohomological corner datum at level $Nr$, together with the unit root $\alpha$ of the Hecke polynomial $X^2-t_pX+p$, to a two-level datum $\mathbb T_a\to\mathbb T_1$ at level $Nrp$ whose $\mathbb T_1$-corner is identified with the $\theta_1$-localised Hecke algebra of level $Np$, with $U_p$ residually equal to the unit root. It is used by [`CuspForm.heckeLocal.exists_h1CornerData_refinement_degeneracy_level_mul_of_cornerData_of_fullCorner_of_trace_sq_ne_of_not_cube_dvd`](thm.html#CuspForm.heckeLocal.exists_h1CornerData_refinement_degeneracy_level_mul_of_cornerData_of_fullCorner_of_trace_sq_ne_of_not_cube_dvd), which assembles the relative two-level corner datum entering the level-lowering and lifting steps.
